Looks like you've been spoiled, so I'm not gonna bother hiding spoiler
info...

You can easily tame 'domestic' animals.  Those are small dogs, dogs, large
dogs, kittens, cat, large cat, ponies, horses, and war horses.  Those
animals are easily tamable by throwing appropriate food at them.  Dogs and
cats are carnivore, so you need to throw some sort of meat thingies (tripe
rations do wonders) at them, while horses are harbivores so you need to
throw fruits and vegetables at them.

For any other monsters, practically speaking, you'll need some kind of
magical way to tame them.

Scrolls of taming, Magical Harps, Charm Monster spell are most practical
ones.

You can also 'create' tame monsters.  Either by hatching eggs (depending on
the situation, you get random result) or by rubbing a figurine of a monster
(depends on the blessed/uncursed/cursed status of the figurine, you get
varying result).  Most popular way to get "useful" eggs are by polymorphing
yourself into a monster, and if you are a female, you can lay eggs.  The
most useful figurines usually comes from wishing one for it.

